boss.brief:
This is not about writing something new. It is about READING five broken programs, diagnosing each from its error, and fixing it. Write the five corrected functions in the editor. Each one has exactly one of the five classic bugs.

1. NameError. Fix the typo so it returns width times height.
   def rectangle_area(width, height):
       return width * hieght

2. TypeError. seat is a number. Make ticket("Niko", 12) return the string: Niko seat 12
   def ticket(name, seat):
       return name + " seat " + seat

3. SyntaxError. Something is missing at the end of the def line. is_even(4) should be True, is_even(3) should be False.
   def is_even(n)
       return n % 2 == 0

4. IndexError. Positions start at 0. second_item(["x", "y"]) should return "y".
   def second_item(items):
       return items[2]

5. ValueError. The text is a price like "9.99". int() refuses a decimal. Make to_price("9.99") return the number 9.99.
   def to_price(text):
       return int(text)

Fix all five and make every check pass. You clear the gauntlet when the console is green.

boss.modelSolution:
def rectangle_area(width, height):
    return width * height

def ticket(name, seat):
    return f"{name} seat {seat}"

def is_even(n):
    return n % 2 == 0

def second_item(items):
    return items[1]

def to_price(text):
    return float(text)
